                <pb facs="0313" n="195" sameAs="frus:frus1929v03/pg195"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">838.00/2624: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The High Commissioner in Haiti</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Russell</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Port-au-Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-12-07T11:00:00-05:00">December 7, 1929—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 4:08 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>97. Department’s 63, December 6, 11 a.m. Verbal order to the brigade commander
                    has been issued for the strict compliance with the instructions contained in the
                    above-mentioned telegram.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Russell</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
